    "text": "We ran an intern expo last summer to help students get jobs for 2027 (and help our companies hire!) and we nerded out with software. We built lookbooks, AI-powered matching, 15-minute speed interviews and a ton more -- using bits to move bodies and make in-person connections.<p>For fun, we also wrote a blog post on how we did it, with a simulation of the event: different variables we tried, and even some easter eggs for each company. (See if you can conjure Garry to the floor!)<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.ycombinator.com&#x2F;software&#x2F;blog&#x2F;yc-unbroke-the-career-fair\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.ycombinator.com&#x2F;software&#x2F;blog&#x2F;yc-unbroke-the-car...</a><p>It&#x27;ll be a slow day when our little YC software blog trends on HN, but I wanted to share -- and that if you like writing software that runs ops, helps people get jobs and generally nerd out with AI, we&#x27;re hiring. Email ryan@ycombinator.com if you&#x27;re interested!<p>More on our software team here:<p><a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.ycombinator.com&#x2F;software\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.ycombinator.com&#x2F;software</a>",
